KAART 004
KODAK FILMSTOCK IDENTIFICATION
The labels on the filmcan  have the following  codes: 
Top                : Light  (3200 K) = colorbalance  tungsten.
                   : Sun    (5600 K) = colorbalance  daylight.
Filter No 85  : Correction filter for use in daylight.              
Filter No 80a : Correction filter for use in artificial light.
E.L. 500/28   : Exposure rating.
E.L. 320/26   : Exposure rating with filter.
5296          : Filmtype ID number
Bottom        : (Example) 35  N  4740  EI
35   = Film format.
N    = Negative Type
4740 = Metric Perforation Pitch
EI   = Emulsion Position/Winding Type (inside)
U    = On " U" core.
 

KAART 005
FILMSTOCK STORAGE TEMPERATURES
 
In original closed cans,  for color and B/W
max. 6 month at : 13 grads Celsius/55 grads Fahrenheit.
over 6 month between : -18 and -23 graden Celsius
The cans should not be opened before they reach the ambient temperature 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 




